    /** Shape $ (Value): object. Shape $.object (Required): object and {@see CheckoutSessionInput}. A session in which a buyer completes an order's payment. Shape $.object.active_payment_attempt (Optional): {@see OrderPaymentAttemptInput}. An attempt to pay an order. Shape $.object.buyer_contact (Optional): {@see CheckoutBuyerContactInput}. Contact the buyer entered in checkout before paying, saved with the session's checkout credential. Separate from merchant-supplied prefill and customer_prefill from the customer record. Omitted until the buyer saves or clears a field. When a checkout session payment omits buyer_contact.email or buyer_contact.phone, Flint uses these values. Flint clears the contact 30 days after the session ends, and when a customer linked to the session is deleted. Buyer contact supplied with payment or saved during checkout. Shape $.object.buyer_fields (Optional): {@see CheckoutBuyerFieldsInput}. What checkout asks the buyer for. Each field you leave out uses your checkout settings. Shape $.object.can_save_payment_method (Optional): boolean. Whether checkout offers the buyer the option to save the card they type for faster checkout at this merchant. When true and save_payment_method_requires_verification is false, PayOrder accepts save_payment_method: true for one newly collected card. False when the merchant turned checkout.saved_payment_details off, customer accounts are merchant hosted, card is not an available payment option, the checkout collects an invoice, a subscription, or a return, or the checkout acts for no customer and Flint cannot email the buyer a verification code. Returned only to the checkout credential; never in webhook payloads. Shape $.object.can_save_payment_method_with_phone (Optional): boolean. Whether the buyer can save the card they type by giving a US or Canadian mobile phone number with the payment, in save_payment_method_phone on POST /v1/orders/{order_id}/pay, and confirming it with a texted code after paying. True while Flint can send texts and either save_payment_method_requires_verification is true, so the number replaces confirming an email before paying, or the checkout acts for the customer whose email the buyer confirmed with this credential, so the number joins that customer's saved details once the buyer confirms it. Returned only to the checkout credential; never in webhook payloads. Shape $.object.checkout_session_id (Required): string. Shape $.object.closed_reason_message (Optional): string. The note supplied when the checkout session was closed. Shape $.object.created_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.custom_text (Optional): {@see CheckoutCustomTextConfigInput}. Custom text shown in checkout: an order summary message and a shipping address label. Shape $.object.customer (Optional): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput} or null. Shape $.object.customer.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput}. A customer's summary fields, returned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. Shape $.object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. Shape $.object.customer_id (Optional): string. The customer of the session's order. Omitted when the order has none. A checkout credential issued for this session acts for this customer. Add expand=customer to include the customer. Shape $.object.customer_prefill (Optional): {@see CheckoutCustomerPrefillInput}. Contact and default addresses of the customer the checkout acts for, with the recipient name on its default shipping address: the customer the merchant created the session for, or the customer whose email the buyer confirmed in it. Present on GET and PATCH responses while the session is open and acts for a customer. Separate from merchant-supplied prefill and buyer_contact saved by the buyer. Returned only to the checkout credential; never in webhook payloads. Details the buyer's checkout can prefill from the customer it acts for. Shape $.object.delivery (Optional): {@see CheckoutDerivedDeliveryResourceInput}. Current delivery choices for Flint-owned pricing. External pricing reports requires_explicit_quote; reading this field does not request a delivery quote. Omitted when the session is not open, has no order, or Flint cannot read its delivery. The delivery options Flint derived for a checkout as a buyer sees them: choice groups, input requirements, and evaluation status. Shape $.object.delivery_method_ids (Required): Array of string. Immutable delivery method assignment captured when the checkout was created. Shape $.object.delivery_method_ids[] (Value): string. Shape $.object.delivery_pinned_dependencies (Optional): Array of {@see CheckoutDeliveryPinnedDependencyInput}. Immutable configuration lineage used to evaluate delivery quotes. Shape $.object.delivery_pinned_dependencies[] (Value): {@see CheckoutDeliveryPinnedDependencyInput}. A delivery dependency pinned to a checkout, such as the assigned method, eligibility, or pricing callback, with the revision it was pinned at. Shape $.object.delivery_selection_required (Required): boolean. Whether the order has at least one remaining quote-resolved fulfillment choice that must be selected before payment. Shape $.object.expires_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.expires_in_seconds (Optional): integer string. The lifetime the session got. expires_at is its deadline. Omitted for invoice sessions, which take their deadline from the invoice. Use an integer string (decimal digits), not a floating-point number. Format: int64. Shape $.object.external_reference_id (Optional): string. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. maxLength: 255. Shape $.object.gift_card_challenge (Optional): {@see CheckoutGiftCardChallengeInput}. Where the buyer completes a gift card challenge for this checkout. Returned on single-session reads, session create and update responses, checkout launch results, and customer verification confirmation results while the session is open and can show the challenge. Omitted from lists, webhooks, expanded resources, and delivery selection results. A URL to load in an iframe when applying a gift card returns `GIFT_CARD_CHALLENGE_REQUIRED`. Shape $.object.invoice (Optional): {@see ExpandedInvoiceSummaryInput} or null. Shape $.object.invoice.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedInvoiceSummaryInput}. An invoice's summary fields, including status, due date, and paid, outstanding, and refunded amounts, returned when the invoice is expanded. Shape $.object.invoice.anyOf[2] (Value): null. Shape $.object.invoice_id (Optional): string. Shape $.object.is_in_recovery (Required): boolean. Whether this terminal session credential is temporarily restricted to recovering its owning payment attempt. Shape $.object.legal (Optional): {@see CheckoutLegalConfigInput}. Legal settings for a checkout: whether buyers must accept terms, and links to the terms, refund policy, shipping policy, and contract. Shape $.object.merchant_icon (Optional): {@see ImageInput}. The merchant's square icon, shown in browser tabs and compact headers. Returned by `GET /v1/checkout-sessions/{checkout_session_id}` when the merchant has one; other responses and webhooks omit it. An image with its `url`, `width`, and `height`, and optional `alt` text. Shape $.object.merchant_id (Optional): string. Shape $.object.merchant_logo (Optional): {@see ImageInput}. The merchant's logo. Returned by `GET /v1/checkout-sessions/{checkout_session_id}` when the merchant has one; other responses and webhooks omit it. An image with its `url`, `width`, and `height`, and optional `alt` text. Shape $.object.merchant_name (Optional): string. The merchant's business name, which hosted checkout shows when `theme.title` is unset. Reads `Merchant` when the merchant has not set a business name. Returned by `GET /v1/checkout-sessions/{checkout_session_id}`; other responses and webhooks omit it. Shape $.object.merchant_support (Optional): {@see CheckoutMerchantSupportInput}. How the buyer can reach the merchant for help: the support email, phone, and URL the merchant set. Present on GET and PATCH responses when the merchant set at least one of them. Show it where your checkout tells the buyer to contact the merchant, such as an expired or closed checkout, or your receipt. Returned only to the checkout credential; never in webhook payloads. The merchant's support contact. Each field is omitted when the merchant has not set it. Shape $.object.metadata (Optional): {@see MetadataMapInput}. Caller-owned key-value data stored on a resource. Keys starting with flint_ are reserved for Flint and are not returned. Writes follow the limits on MetadataInput and MetadataPatchInput; maps written before those limits may not satisfy them. Shape $.object.order (Optional): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput} or null. Shape $.object.order.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput}. An order's summary fields, including status, payment and refund status, and pricing and settlement amounts, returned when the order is expanded. Shape $.object.order.anyOf[2] (Value): null. Shape $.object.order_id (Optional): string. Shape $.object.page_origin (Optional): string. Origin of the page that renders this embedded checkout. Omitted when not set. Shape $.object.payment_collection (Optional): {@see PaymentCollectionInput}. Guidance for collecting a payment source. Checkout-credential reads include it only while the session is open. Returned only to the checkout credential; never in webhook payloads. Client-side details for collecting payment from the buyer, such as the Stripe settings to initialize Stripe.js. Shape $.object.payment_intent_ids (Optional): Array of string. Shape $.object.payment_intent_ids[] (Value): string. Shape $.object.payment_intents (Optional): Array of {@see ExpandedPaymentIntentSummaryInput}. Shape $.object.payment_intents[] (Value): {@see ExpandedPaymentIntentSummaryInput}. A payment intent's summary fields, including amount, status, and capture method, returned when the payment intent is expanded. Shape $.object.payment_link (Optional): {@see ExpandedPaymentLinkSummaryInput} or null. Shape $.object.payment_link.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedPaymentLinkSummaryInput}. A payment link's summary fields, including name, type, status, and URL, returned when the payment link is expanded. Shape $.object.payment_link.anyOf[2] (Value): null. Shape $.object.payment_link_id (Optional): string. Shape $.object.payment_link_image (Optional): {@see ImageInput}. The current image of the payment link that opened this session. Returned by `GET /v1/checkout-sessions/{checkout_session_id}` when that link has an image; other responses and webhooks omit it. An image with its `url`, `width`, and `height`, and optional `alt` text. Shape $.object.payment_method_save (Optional): {@see CheckoutPaymentMethodSaveInput}. The card the buyer saved with this checkout's payment by giving a mobile phone number, and whether they confirmed it. Present on GET and PATCH responses after a payment that paid the order in full, or that was approved for the merchant to capture later, and saved a card this way. A checkout whose payment is approved stays open until the capture. Returned only to the checkout credential; never in webhook payloads. A card the buyer saved with the checkout's payment by giving a mobile phone number. It works for nothing until the buyer confirms it with a code: request one with POST /v1/checkout-sessions/{checkout_session_id}/customer-verifications and purpose confirm_saved_payment_method. Shape $.object.payment_return_url (Optional): string. Embedded sessions only. Absolute HTTPS URL on your site where Flint sends the buyer after a redirect payment such as Affirm, whatever the outcome; read the session there to show the result. Required when the session offers affirm. It can't contain credentials, a query string, or a fragment. Test mode also accepts http loopback URLs. Up to 2,048 characters. Format: uri. maxLength: 2048. Shape $.object.payments (Optional): {@see CheckoutPaymentConfigInput}. Configured payment options for merchant credentials; currently available payment options for the checkout credential. Payment settings for a checkout: the enabled payment options and a note shown with payment. Shape $.object.prefill (Optional): {@see CheckoutPrefillInput}. Contact details and addresses to fill in for the buyer, who can change them. For a customer with saved addresses, Flint fills in any address you leave out, and reads include it. With quick_pay or subscription_plan and automatic tax on, a prefilled address sets the order's tax location. Not changed by what the buyer types; for that, read buyer_contact. customer_prefill is what the checkout credential reads from the customer record. Shape $.object.problems (Required): Array of {@see CheckoutProblemResourceInput}. Named conditions that affect checkout completion. Follow each problem's remediation action instead of reconstructing delivery lifecycle rules in the client. payment_in_progress means another payment for the order must finish before this checkout can complete. When Flint cannot read the checkout's delivery, the read still succeeds and reports delivery_unreadable; its remediation says whether reading the session again can succeed, and its next action's reason_code names the error. Shape $.object.problems[] (Value): {@see CheckoutProblemResourceInput}. A problem with a checkout session, such as a stale delivery selection, with its `code`, whether it blocks completion, and remediation. Shape $.object.promotion_config (Optional): {@see CheckoutPromotionConfigInput}. Promotion settings for a checkout: whether automatic promotions apply and whether the buyer can apply promotion codes. Shape $.object.recovery_expires_at (Optional): string or null. RFC3339 deadline for the restricted payment-attempt recovery window. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.recovery_payment_attempt_id (Optional): string. Paymen